  "description": "Sola Sound Tone Bender MkII Professional (1966) as Fuzz Central traced an original: three germanium PNPs, positive ground (the supply is -9 V), fixed bias resistors, Level and Attack. OC81Ds as the trace says (an estimate from our OC75 fit, D-184), at the gains Fuzz Central suggests (70, 70 and 100). Aion's Deimos version, with bias trimmers and a Mode switch, is a starter of its own.",
